{
  "text": "```verilog\n`timescale 1ns/1ps\n\nmodule synchronizer #(\n    parameter STAGES = 2\n)(\n    input  wire clk,\n    input  wire rstn,\n    input  wire async_sig_i,\n    output wire sync_sig_o\n);\n\n    wire [STAGES-1:0] sync_pipe;\n\n    genvar i;\n    generate\n        for (i = 0; i < STAGES; i = i + 1) begin : stage_gen\n            assign sync_pipe[i] = sync_pipe[i-1];\n        end\n    endgenerate\n\n    // Handle the first stage separately to handle the initial reset state correctly\n    // and chain the rest.\n    // Stage 0: Input -> Flip Flop\n    // Stage 1 to STAGES-1: Chain Flip Flops\n    \n    // We need to ensure the output is low on reset.\n    // Since rstn is active low, we use ~rstn for logic high enable.\n    \n    // First stage\n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rstn) begin\n        if (!rstn)\n            sync_pipe[0] <= 1'b0;\n        else\n            sync_pipe[0] <= async_sig_i;\n    end\n\n    // Subsequent stages\n    genvar j;\n    generate\n        for (j = 1; j < STAGES; j = j + 1) begin : stage_gen_sub\n            always @(posedge clk or negedge rstn) begin\n                if (!rstn)\n                    sync_pipe[j] <= 1'b0;\n                else\n                    sync_pipe[j] <= sync_pipe[j-1];\n            end\n        end\n    endgenerate\n\n    assign sync_sig_o = sync_pipe[STAGES-1];\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
